# Team Brain — shared agent memory (mandatory loop)

If this workspace has `.team-brain/` (credentials / cache) **or** the user is working on a shared Jira initiative / spike / epic, you MUST treat Team Brain as the crew’s shared memory.

Personal `BRAIN.md` / engineer-brain stay private — never upload those.

## Mandatory loop (do not skip)

```text
BEFORE deep research / exploration on a Jira key
  → recall (sync) team memories for that key
  → prefer .team-brain/cache/<KEY>.json
  → summarize what the crew already knows
  → only then dig into the codebase

AFTER you learn something durable (path, decision, constraint, “start here”)
  → remember it immediately with a stable source_ref
  → do not wait for the user to say “save this”
```

### How to run (prefer MCP `team-brain` tools if connected)

```bash
# Before research — sync
bash <engineer-brain>/core/scripts/team-brain-api.sh recall <JIRA-KEY>
bash <engineer-brain>/core/scripts/team-brain-api.sh recall <JIRA-KEY> "<topic>"

# After research — save (source_ref avoids dupes across laptops)
bash <engineer-brain>/core/scripts/team-brain-api.sh remember <JIRA-KEY> research --source-ref "<JIRA-KEY>#<short-slug>" "<finding>"
```

If the skill scripts are installed under `.cursor/skills/team-brain/scripts/`, use that path instead.

## Parallel engineers (two laptops)

- Ada’s `remember` only helps Bob after Bob’s agent runs `recall` (or `watch` refreshed cache).
- Your job on Bob’s machine: **recall first** so you do not re-research Ada’s work.
- Your job after you find something: **remember immediately** so Ada does not re-research yours.

## Never

- Start a large exploratory pass on a known Jira key without `recall`
- Leave durable findings only in chat
- Put personal career / performance notes into Team Brain
- Commit or paste `credentials.json` / `api_key`
